Package: usb-blacklist-watcher-pve
Version: 1.1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: albeph
Depends: bash (>= 4.0), inotify-tools
Recommends: proxmox-ve
Provides: usb-blacklist-watcher
Replaces: usb-blacklist-watcher
Conflicts: usb-blacklist-watcher
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: USB device passthrough blacklist enforcer for Proxmox VE
 Prevents specific USB devices from being assigned (passed through) to any
 QEMU/KVM virtual machine on a Proxmox VE host node — whether the VM is
 running or stopped, and whether the assignment is done via the GUI, the
 CLI, or any other means.
 .
 The package installs two tools:
  - usb-blacklist-select: an interactive CLI to choose which USB devices to
    protect, with non-interactive --add/--remove/--list flags for scripting.
  - usb-blacklist-watcher-pve: a systemd daemon that monitors VM configuration
    files via inotify and immediately removes any blacklisted USB entries
    using `qm set <VMID> --delete usbN`, supporting both hot-unplug (running
    VMs) and static config edits (stopped VMs).
 .
 The blacklist is stored in /etc/usb-blacklist-watcher-pve/blacklist.conf and
 uses vendor:product ID format (e.g. 2e8a:0005) for reliable matching
 regardless of which USB port a device is plugged into.
